Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes. It learns numeric-field patterns and repeating text templates, then arithmetic-codes exceptions; all reconstruction metadata is stored in the compressed file, with general-purpose fallbacks for other inputs. The 313,972-byte corpus compresses to 2,909 bytes—a 99.0735% reduction, versus 35,399 bytes for default zlib—and restores byte-identically. The registered assay passed three runs with zero score variation; 100 arithmetic-coder tests and additional fallback round trips also passed.